  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "For each of our 40 kidney cancer patients I need one number per transcription factor that captures that TF's regulatory strength in that patient, so we can relate it to survival. We have expression, a motif prior and a TF-TF PPI. I'm honestly not sure whether 'regulatory strength' here should mean how strongly the TF is wired to its targets or how active the TF is; my PI used both phrasings."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"one number per transcription factor that captures that TF's regulatory strength in that patient\" -- available from GIRAFFE.\n\n**GIRAFFE**. GIRAFFE jointly factors expression into a regulatory-effect matrix and sample-varying TF activities using biological priors. Signed effects describe the fitted activation/repression relationship, while activity differs from the TF's own expression. These fitted coefficients do not alone establish causality.\n\nYou would need expression matrix, motif/prior, PPI network. The analysis would provide inferred regulator-to-target associations; inferred transcription-factor-by-sample activity values.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
